    {
      "id": "712971fc-0664-5b46-b38c-4b1b29c8ed0d",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Deserted-lot triage\nA lot nobody bid for forces a negotiated procedure and the need is still there. Each week this finds new deserted lots, has Claude classify the likely reason with the hospital's own rules (structural / earlier decision / addressable) and routes each to the owner who can act.\n\n**Data:** public PLACSP results via Licita, anonymised. **Guardrails:** routing informs, it doesn't decide; unreadable or unsupported cases go to Procurement as `unclear`; every lot is logged once.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 360,
        "color": "5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f1809e22-df60-5dc5-88ea-9fc7e2164efa",
      "name": "Idempotent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1120,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Never twice\n`Not triaged yet` checks the `deserted_triage` table, so a lot is classified and emailed once, however often the workflow runs.",
        "width": 420,
        "height": 220,
        "color": "4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f2e0e5b1-21ce-510d-8930-d73a08f58c20",
      "name": "Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2160,
        -440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Who acts\nStructural → Procurement (check exclusivity, negotiated procedure). Earlier decision → Procurement with the equipment owner. Addressable → the requesting unit (market consultation, budget, lots). Unclear → Procurement for a manual look.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200,
        "color": "6"
      }
    }
  ],
